  "cil_liability": true,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Prior to the first occupation of the development hereby permitted, the proposed cycle store indicated within Drawing No. 003 Revision 05 (Proposed Site Plan) and 301 Revision 00 (Proposed Bike Storage) shall have been fully provided on site, and shall thereafter be retained in perpetuity\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to conform to Enfield DMD policy 45 and promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rApplication Form,\rDesign & Access Document,\rDaylight, Sunlight & Overshadowing Assessment,\rPlanning Statement,\rTransport Technical Note,\r001 Revision 01 (Site Location Plan),\r002 Revision 03 (Existing Site Plan),\r003 Revision 05 (Proposed Site Plan),\r101 Revision 02 (Existing Ground Floor Plan),\r102 Revision 02 (Existing First Floor Plan),\r103 Revision 02 (Existing Second Floor Plan),\r104 Revision 02 (Existing Roof Plan),\r121 Revision 02 (Existing Front and Rear Elevations),\r122 Revision 02 (Existing Side Elevations),\r210 Revision 06 (Proposed Third Floor Plan),\r211 Revision 02 (Proposed Roof Plan), \r221 Revision 02 (Proposed Front and Rear Elevations),\r222 Revision 02 (Proposed Side Elevations),\r230 Revision 00 (Existing and Proposed Sections),\r301 Revision 00 (Proposed Bike Storage),\r501 Revision 00 (Wall Junction Detail).\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, details of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to be provided within the development, in accordance with the London Borough of Enfield Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024), shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The facilities shall be provided in accordance with the approved details before the development is occupied or use commences and maintained as such thereafter.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The development, including demolition of the existing structures on site, shall not commence until a construction management plan has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rThe construction management plan shall be written in accordance with London Best Practice Guidance and contain: \ra) A photographic condition survey of the public roads, footways and verges leading to the site. \rb) Details of construction access and associated traffic management. \rc) Arrangements for the loading, unloading, and turning of delivery, construction, and service vehicles. \rd) Arrangements for the parking of contractors' vehicles. \re) Arrangements for the storage of materials. \rf) Hours of work. \rg) Arrangements for deliveries. \rh) The storage and removal of excavation material. \ri) Measures to reduce danger to cyclists. \rj) Measures to control the emission of dust and dirt during the demolition and construction in accordance with the Mayor of London's supplementary planning guidance 'The Control of Dust and Emissions During Construction and Demolition. \r \rThe development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved construction management plan unless otherwise agreed by the Local Planning Authority.  The approved plan shall be fully implemented for the duration of any demolition and construction works.  All Non-Road Mobile Machinery of net power 37kW and up to and including 560kW used during the course of the demolition, site preparation and construction phases shall comply with the emission standards set out in chapter 7 of the GLA's SPG, or subsequent guidance. Unless it complies with the standards set out in the SPG, no NRMM shall be on site, at any time, whether in use or not, without the prior written consent of the local planning authority. The developer shall keep an up to date list of all NRMM used during the demolition, site preparation and construction phases of the development on the online register at https://nrmm.london/\r\rReason: To ensure construction does not lead to damage of the nearby public road network and to protect local amenity and minimise disruption to the neighbouring properties.\r"
  ]
